1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:01,967
<i>Help! Call an ambulance, quick!</i>

2
00:00:02,100 --> 00:00:03,267
<i> What happened to Andrew?</i>

3
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:06,000
<i>We found him being attacked
by two men.</i>

4
00:00:06,133 --> 00:00:07,967
<i>You know,
I have an idea who did this.</i>

5
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:09,167
<i>I thought you were going
to meet your friend.</i>

6
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:10,900
<i>It's cancelled.
No meeting tonight.</i>

7
00:00:11,033 --> 00:00:12,767
<i> Jin Ho wouldn't do this to us.</i>

8
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:14,067
<i> If not him, then who?</i>

9
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:17,800
<i>I have no idea who did this
to my brother.</i>

10
00:00:17,933 --> 00:00:20,967
<i>He should be careful
who he crosses next time.</i>

11
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:22,667
<i> Strict orders from Ma'am Zoey.</i>

12
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:23,800
<i> No one can enter.</i>

13
00:00:23,933 --> 00:00:25,333
<i> Hey, Zoey, come out!</i>

14
00:00:25,467 --> 00:00:27,400
<i>There's no chance
Andrew will fall</i>

15
00:00:27,533 --> 00:00:29,867
<i> for an immature kid like you.</i>

16
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,133
<i> Joey...</i>

17
00:00:49,467 --> 00:00:52,300
Zoey, we're here as Andrew's
friends.

18
00:00:52,533 --> 00:00:54,433
We just want to check on him.

19
00:00:54,567 --> 00:00:56,200
Keep telling yourself that.

20
00:00:56,333 --> 00:00:57,400
But in the meantime,

21
00:00:57,533 --> 00:00:59,633
I have a patient
to take care of,

22
00:00:59,767 --> 00:01:00,867
so bye.

23
00:01:02,167 --> 00:01:03,200
Go.

24
00:01:04,267 --> 00:01:05,333
Let it go.

25
00:01:06,167 --> 00:01:16,133
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

26
00:01:21,733 --> 00:01:22,900
Andrew?

27
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:25,100
You're awake. Wait...

28
00:01:25,233 --> 00:01:27,500
- I'll call the doctor.
- Zoey...

29
00:01:27,633 --> 00:01:29,133
[GROANS]

30
00:01:29,267 --> 00:01:31,000
Why? Are you okay?

31
00:01:31,133 --> 00:01:32,133
I'm okay.

32
00:01:32,267 --> 00:01:34,833
Zoey, what happened when I lost
consciousness?

33
00:01:34,967 --> 00:01:37,133
Is Joey here?

34
00:01:37,267 --> 00:01:41,967
She was with me
before everything went black.

35
00:01:42,133 --> 00:01:44,467
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

36
00:01:47,267 --> 00:01:48,267
Yes.

37
00:01:49,367 --> 00:01:52,000
She brought you here
to the hospital.

38
00:01:52,133 --> 00:01:54,233
She stayed until you were
admitted.

39
00:01:54,367 --> 00:01:56,167
But then, after that...

40
00:01:57,500 --> 00:01:58,700
She left,

41
00:01:58,833 --> 00:02:00,833
and she hasn't come back
until now.

42
00:02:00,967 --> 00:02:03,700
Maybe she has more important
things to attend to.

43
00:02:03,833 --> 00:02:05,533
And honestly,

44
00:02:06,633 --> 00:02:08,767
that's probably for the best.

45
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:10,933
What do you mean, Zoey?

46
00:02:13,967 --> 00:02:16,733
Andrew, let's be real, okay?

47
00:02:18,367 --> 00:02:23,200
If she hadn't forced you
to meet and go out,

48
00:02:23,333 --> 00:02:24,900
this wouldn't have happened.

49
00:02:25,033 --> 00:02:27,367
You wouldn't be hurt like this.
Look at you.

50
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:28,467
Zoey...

51
00:02:29,567 --> 00:02:31,567
No one wanted this to happen.

52
00:02:31,700 --> 00:02:33,433
It's not Joey's fault.

53
00:02:33,567 --> 00:02:34,967
You're still defending her?

54
00:02:35,100 --> 00:02:37,100
I'm stating facts.

55
00:02:37,233 --> 00:02:39,167
You shouldn't be blaming her.

56
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:40,867
You know what? Okay.

57
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:42,667
But enough about her for now.

58
00:02:42,800 --> 00:02:44,800
You need to be checked
by a doctor.

59
00:02:44,933 --> 00:02:46,667
That's what matters right now.

60
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:48,300
Wait, I'll call them.

61
00:02:48,467 --> 00:02:49,433
Stay put.

62
00:02:49,567 --> 00:02:56,100
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

63
00:02:57,800 --> 00:03:01,067
Forget what Zoey said.

64
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:03,100
Don't be sad.
[GLUM MUSIC PLAYING]

65
00:03:03,233 --> 00:03:05,633
You look like a pitiful
street kid.

66
00:03:09,433 --> 00:03:12,367
A beautiful street kid.

67
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:13,833
You didn't let me finish.

68
00:03:13,967 --> 00:03:15,767
There, be careful what you say.

69
00:03:15,900 --> 00:03:19,400
Why am I even thinking
about what Zoey said?

70
00:03:19,533 --> 00:03:23,000
Forget it.
Her words don't matter.

71
00:03:23,167 --> 00:03:24,767
"Forget it"? Really?

72
00:03:24,900 --> 00:03:27,200
You were the one who made
a scene earlier.

73
00:03:27,333 --> 00:03:30,067
Of course, I didn't want you
to be at a disadvantage.

74
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:31,900
You know, I'll just think...

75
00:03:32,967 --> 00:03:36,600
I'm happy Andrew is awake
and recovering.

76
00:03:36,733 --> 00:03:39,767
Good. Let's stay positive...

77
00:03:39,900 --> 00:03:43,633
Unless you want us
to make a distraction.

78
00:03:43,767 --> 00:03:46,700
Do you want to sneak
into Andrew's room?

79
00:03:46,833 --> 00:03:47,633
No.

80
00:03:47,767 --> 00:03:50,533
We might get banned
from the hospital.

81
00:03:50,667 --> 00:03:53,100
And if Zoey finds out,

82
00:03:53,233 --> 00:03:55,367
she'll say all sorts
of things again.

83
00:03:55,533 --> 00:03:56,967
Then we'll just say...

84
00:03:58,233 --> 00:03:59,900
"Sorry."

85
00:04:00,600 --> 00:04:02,700
You're really nuts, you know?
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

86
00:04:02,833 --> 00:04:04,567
The nuts who made you smile.

87
00:04:04,700 --> 00:04:05,600
Sorry, sorry.

88
00:04:05,733 --> 00:04:08,333
Let's leave now
because you're annoying me.

89
00:04:08,467 --> 00:04:09,267
Sorry.

90
00:04:09,400 --> 00:04:11,233
- Do it one more time.
- No.

91
00:04:11,367 --> 00:04:12,933
- I'll choke you.
- Sorry.

92
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:16,167
Kyle, I'm telling you...

93
00:04:16,300 --> 00:04:17,967
that is not random.

94
00:04:18,100 --> 00:04:20,367
Someone wants to hurt
or kill Andrew.

95
00:04:20,500 --> 00:04:22,100
We can't just let this slide.

96
00:04:22,233 --> 00:04:23,633
Madam, I was thinking...

97
00:04:23,767 --> 00:04:25,067
What if we give a reward

98
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:27,200
<i>to whoever identifies
Boss Andrew's assailants?</i>

99
00:04:27,367 --> 00:04:28,867
Do we have budget?

100
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,667
I have 500 pesos here.

101
00:04:30,800 --> 00:04:32,667
<i> Wow, that's a big help.</i>

102
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:35,500
<i>You know, let's talk about it
when I get there. Wait for me.</i>

103
00:04:35,633 --> 00:04:37,433
I'll just finish this
for publishing.

104
00:04:37,567 --> 00:04:39,867
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

105
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:41,900
Kyle? Hello? Hey.

106
00:04:42,033 --> 00:04:42,767
Hello, hello?

107
00:04:42,900 --> 00:04:44,900
Sorry, I saw Joey.

108
00:04:45,033 --> 00:04:47,367
Maybe she visited Andrew.

109
00:04:47,500 --> 00:04:50,267
He's indeed a "Boss Idol."

110
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:51,667
All right, all right.

111
00:04:55,367 --> 00:04:57,000
Let's go, Kyle.

112
00:04:57,133 --> 00:04:59,000
- Andrew, Kyle's here.
- Boss?

113
00:04:59,133 --> 00:05:02,900
- Boss! Boss, I missed you!
- Ouch, ouch, ouch...

114
00:05:03,067 --> 00:05:05,233
Sorry, sorry.

115
00:05:05,367 --> 00:05:09,433
I just missed you and I'm happy
you're okay now.

116
00:05:09,567 --> 00:05:10,933
You're fine, right?

117
00:05:11,067 --> 00:05:14,333
- Yes.
- Sorry, sorry.

118
00:05:14,467 --> 00:05:15,533
Boss...

119
00:05:16,667 --> 00:05:21,167
Guys, I'll buy food downstairs.
Do you want anything? Andrew?

120
00:05:21,300 --> 00:05:24,033
For me, pancake and coffee,
Zoey.

121
00:05:25,367 --> 00:05:29,933
You already hurt the patient,
now you want his food.

122
00:05:31,567 --> 00:05:34,133
Sorry, sorry. Yes, Boss.
[CHEEKY MUSIC PLAYING]

123
00:05:34,300 --> 00:05:36,000
All right, what do you want?

124
00:05:36,133 --> 00:05:39,367
I'll just get coffee
and pancakes for everyone,

125
00:05:39,500 --> 00:05:42,300
and for Elai too
if she's coming.

126
00:05:42,433 --> 00:05:43,833
Thank you, thank you, Zoey.

127
00:05:43,967 --> 00:05:45,633
Wait for me. I'll buy it quick.

128
00:05:45,767 --> 00:05:49,900
[CHEEKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

129
00:05:52,367 --> 00:05:54,933
Boss, your bouncers outside
are extremely stern.

130
00:05:55,067 --> 00:05:58,367
Really strict. They're scary.

131
00:05:58,500 --> 00:06:04,033
Good thing Zoey
didn't block Joey

132
00:06:04,167 --> 00:06:06,100
from visiting you.

133
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:09,300
Joey visited me?
[CURIOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

134
00:06:09,433 --> 00:06:11,867
Yes, I saw her downstairs,
leaving.

135
00:06:14,233 --> 00:06:15,133
[GRUNTS]

136
00:06:15,267 --> 00:06:16,500
My cellphone.

137
00:06:16,633 --> 00:06:17,667
Why?

138
00:06:18,800 --> 00:06:21,100
I thought she came here,
didn't she?

139
00:06:21,733 --> 00:06:23,867
My phone's dead.

140
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:28,467
No, Zoey told me
she hasn't come back.

141
00:06:30,133 --> 00:06:32,067
Wait, do you have a charger?

142
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:33,633
I don't have one, Boss.

143
00:06:33,767 --> 00:06:39,400
So, Joey came here,
then just left?

144
00:06:39,533 --> 00:06:41,133
Or...

145
00:06:41,300 --> 00:06:44,967
Someone stopped her so you
wouldn't see each other.

146
00:06:45,100 --> 00:06:48,033
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

147
00:06:48,167 --> 00:06:49,500
<i> Bye, Mom!</i>

148
00:06:49,633 --> 00:06:51,067
- Take care, okay?
- Yes.

149
00:06:51,200 --> 00:06:52,867
Take care of yourselves, please.

150
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:55,567
- Let's go. Bye-bye.
- I love you.

151
00:07:08,533 --> 00:07:11,267
Aren't you going to tell them
what happened to Andrew?

152
00:07:11,400 --> 00:07:12,700
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

153
00:07:12,833 --> 00:07:15,533
I don't think it's necessary.

154
00:07:15,700 --> 00:07:17,967
They've already been through
so much with mommy.

155
00:07:18,100 --> 00:07:22,000
And I don't want them worrying
more than they have to.

156
00:07:24,267 --> 00:07:26,600
And lately...

157
00:07:26,733 --> 00:07:28,333
I barely see them.

158
00:07:28,467 --> 00:07:31,033
It's always hospital for mom,

159
00:07:31,167 --> 00:07:33,533
and then another hospital
for Andrew.

160
00:07:33,667 --> 00:07:35,200
You know, and repeat.

161
00:07:35,333 --> 00:07:37,567
I can't fit them
into my schedule anymore.

162
00:07:37,700 --> 00:07:40,367
Well, that's because you've been
running on fumes.

163
00:07:41,500 --> 00:07:43,100
And honestly,

164
00:07:43,233 --> 00:07:45,567
I don't think you deserve
this kind of pressure.

165
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:48,000
Well...

166
00:07:48,167 --> 00:07:53,600
Andrew will be discharged soon,
but I don't know about mom.

167
00:07:53,733 --> 00:07:56,500
I don't know what the next step
is for her.

168
00:07:58,800 --> 00:08:01,000
Well, I've been thinking
about that.

169
00:08:01,133 --> 00:08:04,633
Why don't we explore
private care for her?

170
00:08:04,767 --> 00:08:07,200
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

171
00:08:07,333 --> 00:08:08,567
Private care?

172
00:08:08,700 --> 00:08:09,667
Yes.

173
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:14,000
A quieter place away
from the hospital setting.

174
00:08:14,133 --> 00:08:17,200
Somewhere with more space,
more greenery.

175
00:08:17,333 --> 00:08:20,933
It would be good for her
and for you too.

176
00:08:21,100 --> 00:08:24,500
Wouldn't that be like abandoning
mommy?

177
00:08:24,633 --> 00:08:28,300
As if I'm choosing convenience
over being present?

178
00:08:30,100 --> 00:08:31,867
You're not abandoning her.

179
00:08:33,033 --> 00:08:36,467
You're making sure she's being
taken care of.

180
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:40,567
That way, she gets more rest,
and you too.

181
00:08:42,667 --> 00:08:44,267
The kids miss you.

182
00:08:45,300 --> 00:08:48,267
I miss you too.

183
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:54,200
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

184
00:08:55,300 --> 00:08:56,267
Thank you.

185
00:08:56,400 --> 00:08:57,900
Hey, here's your order!

186
00:08:58,033 --> 00:09:00,500
Pancakes and coffee
for everyone!

187
00:09:00,633 --> 00:09:02,633
- Thank you!
- Kyle, this is yours, okay?

188
00:09:02,767 --> 00:09:04,400
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]
All right, Zoey.

189
00:09:04,533 --> 00:09:07,333
I'll just take out mine
and Elai's.

190
00:09:07,467 --> 00:09:08,367
Take it out?

191
00:09:08,500 --> 00:09:09,200
Yes.

192
00:09:09,333 --> 00:09:10,367
Why?

193
00:09:10,500 --> 00:09:12,667
We still have things to finish
at<i> Tirada</i> .

194
00:09:12,800 --> 00:09:14,000
I just remembered.

195
00:09:14,133 --> 00:09:16,933
- Should I take this?
- Yes, yes.

196
00:09:17,067 --> 00:09:18,800
And the coffee,
that's for you two.

197
00:09:18,933 --> 00:09:21,467
All right, thank you!

198
00:09:21,600 --> 00:09:24,967
Boss, get well soon, okay?

199
00:09:25,100 --> 00:09:26,867
The netizens are waiting
for you.

200
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:28,867
They're waiting for Boss Idol.

201
00:09:29,033 --> 00:09:31,900
And just relax there.

202
00:09:32,033 --> 00:09:33,833
Thank you for the breakfast,
Miss Zoey.

203
00:09:33,967 --> 00:09:36,300
- All right, I'll go ahead.
- Okay.

204
00:09:36,433 --> 00:09:37,867
Take care, Kyle.

205
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:39,500
- Okay, good luck.
- Say hi to Elai for me.

206
00:09:39,633 --> 00:09:40,867
Goodbye, goodbye.

207
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:42,633
Okay. Take care.

208
00:09:51,400 --> 00:09:53,800
Kyle's visit was quick,
wasn't it?

209
00:09:54,933 --> 00:09:57,600
Well, I also got you fish
and eggs.

210
00:09:57,733 --> 00:10:01,233
It's good for your healing.
Lean protein, right?

211
00:10:01,400 --> 00:10:03,867
- Zoey.
- Yeah?

212
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:05,600
Did Joey come here?

213
00:10:05,733 --> 00:10:10,167
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

214
00:10:15,367 --> 00:10:17,600
You know, Andrew,
you need to eat a lot

215
00:10:17,733 --> 00:10:18,867
because you were unconscious
for so long.

216
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:20,933
I'm sure you're starving.

217
00:10:21,067 --> 00:10:23,767
- Here, fish and eggs for you.
- I'm asking you.

218
00:10:23,900 --> 00:10:25,067
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

219
00:10:25,200 --> 00:10:28,600
Zoey, was Joey here earlier?

220
00:10:30,100 --> 00:10:32,233
They told me she was here.

221
00:10:33,833 --> 00:10:34,733
Yes.

222
00:10:35,833 --> 00:10:37,100
She was here.

223
00:10:38,400 --> 00:10:39,900
And then you barred her
from going in?

224
00:10:41,800 --> 00:10:44,767
You have no right to do that,
Zoey.

225
00:10:44,900 --> 00:10:46,667
Are you my girlfriend?

226
00:10:50,767 --> 00:10:52,800
Joey, aren't you going to eat?

227
00:10:54,733 --> 00:10:56,267
Can I ask you something?

228
00:10:58,333 --> 00:11:02,333
What Zoey said at the hospital
earlier...

229
00:11:02,467 --> 00:11:03,900
that you like Andrew...

230
00:11:06,133 --> 00:11:07,567
Is that true?

231
00:11:08,533 --> 00:11:13,400
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

232
00:11:13,533 --> 00:11:15,167
[SIGHS]

233
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:21,300
I've noticed that your concern
for him seems different now.

234
00:11:22,400 --> 00:11:26,600
It's deeper than just normal
friendship.

235
00:11:28,767 --> 00:11:32,333
I noticed that when Andrew
was getting beat up,

236
00:11:32,467 --> 00:11:35,867
it seemed you got weaker
more than him.

237
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:40,500
And you kept checking
if he replied.

238
00:11:42,033 --> 00:11:44,467
You're not like that
with other people, Joey.

239
00:11:46,500 --> 00:11:48,333
Not even with me.

240
00:11:48,467 --> 00:11:57,300
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

241
00:11:59,500 --> 00:12:04,000
Andrew, before you get mad
at me, listen first, okay?

242
00:12:04,133 --> 00:12:05,600
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

243
00:12:05,733 --> 00:12:08,267
I am just protecting you
from her.

244
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:10,867
You only get into trouble
because of Joey!

245
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:13,300
Wait, what trouble
are you talking about?

246
00:12:13,433 --> 00:12:15,367
She didn't do anything wrong,
Zoey.

247
00:12:15,533 --> 00:12:17,600
Why do you keep defending her?

248
00:12:17,733 --> 00:12:21,367
Why can't she do no wrong
in your eyes?

249
00:12:21,500 --> 00:12:23,967
Do you have feelings for her?

250
00:12:24,100 --> 00:12:26,200
I don't owe you an answer.

251
00:12:26,333 --> 00:12:27,667
See?

252
00:12:27,800 --> 00:12:30,467
You can't even admit
it to yourself, Andrew!

253
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:33,100
Because you know
you're not right for each other.

254
00:12:33,233 --> 00:12:34,700
You're too different!

255
00:12:36,200 --> 00:12:37,800
Joey is young.

256
00:12:38,967 --> 00:12:40,567
She is naive.

257
00:12:40,700 --> 00:12:42,133
And you...

258
00:12:42,267 --> 00:12:45,167
You're cynical and jaded.

259
00:12:45,300 --> 00:12:47,767
Do you really think she could
keep up with you?

260
00:12:47,900 --> 00:12:50,300
Even if you have feelings
for each other, Andrew,

261
00:12:50,467 --> 00:12:53,367
it will never work.
It will go nowhere!

262
00:12:53,500 --> 00:12:56,833
Andrew, you know deep down
I'm right.

263
00:12:56,967 --> 00:12:58,667
And maybe the universe agrees,

264
00:12:58,800 --> 00:13:00,367
that's why it's giving you
reasons

265
00:13:00,500 --> 00:13:02,433
- to stay away from Joey...
- Stop that!

266
00:13:02,567 --> 00:13:05,233
- Andrew, this is a clear sign!
- I said stop.

267
00:13:05,367 --> 00:13:09,300
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

268
00:13:10,700 --> 00:13:11,900
Leave.

269
00:13:12,033 --> 00:13:13,567
Andrew...

270
00:13:13,700 --> 00:13:15,200
I said leave.

271
00:13:16,600 --> 00:13:18,533
I don't want to hurt you more.

272
00:13:18,667 --> 00:13:20,500
I might say something worse.

273
00:13:20,633 --> 00:13:30,600
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

274
00:13:52,200 --> 00:13:53,567
Peter...

275
00:13:53,700 --> 00:13:55,033
you're leaving?

276
00:13:56,133 --> 00:13:57,500
Yes, I already stayed overnight.

277
00:13:57,633 --> 00:14:01,967
Your parents might not let me
stay further.

278
00:14:02,100 --> 00:14:03,600
I have a plan.

279
00:14:03,733 --> 00:14:05,333
[CURIOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

280
00:14:05,467 --> 00:14:07,900
I don't like that tone.

281
00:14:08,033 --> 00:14:09,833
What is it?

282
00:14:09,967 --> 00:14:13,433
I'm thinking of the best thing
we can do

283
00:14:13,567 --> 00:14:15,500
because Andrew needs us now.

284
00:14:15,933 --> 00:14:19,133
I think we should corner
whoever attacked him.

285
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:22,933
Don't tell me you still think
it's Jin Ho?

286
00:14:23,067 --> 00:14:25,333
Who else but Jin Ho?

287
00:14:25,467 --> 00:14:28,500
Joey, if you really think Jin Ho
ordered the attack on Andrew,

288
00:14:28,667 --> 00:14:30,833
shouldn't you be more afraid
of him?

289
00:14:32,800 --> 00:14:37,433
Peter, we won't be reckless
this time, and we'll have help.

290
00:14:37,567 --> 00:14:39,367
We'll have someone with us?

291
00:14:40,567 --> 00:14:42,033
Dad.

292
00:14:42,167 --> 00:14:44,467
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

293
00:14:44,600 --> 00:14:49,167
[PHONE RINGING]

294
00:14:49,300 --> 00:14:51,633
Bro, what happened?

295
00:14:51,767 --> 00:14:53,933
I've been messaging you
since last night.

296
00:14:54,067 --> 00:14:57,033
Jin Ho, someone wants to talk
to you.

297
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:00,267
Jin Ho...

298
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:01,933
<i>This is Joey.
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING]</i>

299
00:15:02,100 --> 00:15:04,067
Andrew was attacked yesterday.

300
00:15:04,200 --> 00:15:06,000
He's at the hospital right now.

301
00:15:06,133 --> 00:15:07,400
What?

302
00:15:07,533 --> 00:15:09,767
Jin Ho, we need your help.

303
00:15:09,900 --> 00:15:12,067
We don't know who else
we can trust.

304
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:13,567
Can we meet again?

305
00:15:13,700 --> 00:15:15,900
[BRAZEN MUSIC CONTINUES]

306
00:15:18,100 --> 00:15:19,167
<i> Is everything okay, Zoey?</i>

307
00:15:19,900 --> 00:15:20,700
Yes, Sir.

308
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:24,167
I was supposed to take care
of someone,

309
00:15:24,300 --> 00:15:26,567
but I'm no longer needed.

310
00:15:26,700 --> 00:15:28,967
So, I'll be back on active duty
tomorrow.

311
00:15:29,100 --> 00:15:30,633
<i> Okay, copy that.</i>

312
00:15:30,767 --> 00:15:32,767
<i>We will expect you in briefing.</i>

313
00:15:32,900 --> 00:15:34,467
Understood, Sir.

314
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:35,867
Thank you.

315
00:15:39,967 --> 00:15:42,167
<i>You have no right to do that,
Zoey.</i>

316
00:15:42,300 --> 00:15:43,733
<i> Are you my girlfriend?</i>

317
00:15:44,900 --> 00:15:46,000
<i> Leave.</i>

318
00:15:46,133 --> 00:15:48,033
<i> I don't want to hurt you more.</i>

319
00:15:48,167 --> 00:15:50,033
<i> I might say something worse.</i>

320
00:15:51,500 --> 00:15:59,867
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

321
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:03,700
[REVVING]

322
00:16:06,433 --> 00:16:08,000
How are you?

323
00:16:08,167 --> 00:16:10,633
That wound on your head
looks big.

324
00:16:10,767 --> 00:16:13,133
Doesn't it hurt?

325
00:16:13,267 --> 00:16:14,700
I'm fine, Mom.

326
00:16:14,833 --> 00:16:16,933
- Are you sure?
- Yes.

327
00:16:17,067 --> 00:16:18,100
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

328
00:16:18,233 --> 00:16:20,367
Mom, your concern for me
is overwhelming.

329
00:16:21,833 --> 00:16:24,133
Do you remember me now, Mom?

330
00:16:24,267 --> 00:16:28,367
I remember you always
pestering me here.

331
00:16:28,500 --> 00:16:31,000
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

332
00:16:33,667 --> 00:16:36,500
Actually, mom is doing better.

333
00:16:36,633 --> 00:16:39,867
Aside from her memory loss,
she's more stable.

334
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:41,867
So, I was thinking

335
00:16:42,033 --> 00:16:46,633
maybe it's time to move her
somewhere more peaceful.

336
00:16:48,500 --> 00:16:50,033
More peaceful?

337
00:16:50,167 --> 00:16:51,033
Yes.

338
00:16:51,167 --> 00:16:55,533
Somewhere quiet,
somewhere close to nature.

339
00:16:55,667 --> 00:16:59,700
I was thinking, in one of our
rest houses?

340
00:16:59,833 --> 00:17:02,833
Wait, you mean mommy
will be away from us?

341
00:17:02,967 --> 00:17:04,400
A bit.

342
00:17:04,533 --> 00:17:08,300
There will be nurses
and caregivers there, Andrew,

343
00:17:08,433 --> 00:17:14,033
and Tomas already arranged
an on-call doctor for mom.

344
00:17:15,067 --> 00:17:17,967
This was your idea?
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

345
00:17:18,100 --> 00:17:22,700
We just want to give you
a quieter place to recover, Mom.

346
00:17:22,833 --> 00:17:24,767
You deserve it.

347
00:17:24,900 --> 00:17:26,200
<i> I don't think so.</i>

348
00:17:27,233 --> 00:17:29,167
Mom condition just stabilized
recently.

349
00:17:30,200 --> 00:17:35,433
I think it's better if she stays
here where she's close to us.

350
00:17:35,567 --> 00:17:38,833
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

351
00:17:38,967 --> 00:17:40,200
Andrew,

352
00:17:41,900 --> 00:17:43,633
I want to go.

353
00:17:43,767 --> 00:17:46,100
I don't want to stay
in the hospital anymore.

354
00:17:46,233 --> 00:17:48,567
I'm tired of this hospital bed.

355
00:17:50,167 --> 00:17:52,067
I want to go, son.

356
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:55,700
If that's what you want, Mom.

357
00:17:58,967 --> 00:18:01,567
[ENGINE STARTS]

358
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:06,667
[BEEPING]

359
00:18:07,700 --> 00:18:16,633
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

360
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:29,067
[REVVING]

361
00:18:39,900 --> 00:18:41,967
Wait, Joey, I forgot my wallet.

362
00:18:42,100 --> 00:18:43,167
Hold on, wait.

363
00:18:43,300 --> 00:18:44,567
Hurry up.

364
00:18:47,533 --> 00:18:57,500
[ROMANTIC MUSIC PLAYING]

365
00:19:13,167 --> 00:19:14,367
Andrew!

366
00:19:14,500 --> 00:19:24,467
[ROMANTIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

367
00:19:40,600 --> 00:19:49,933
[HEART POUNDING]

368
00:19:50,933 --> 00:19:55,667
[ROMANTIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

369
00:19:58,233 --> 00:20:03,933
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

370
00:20:09,333 --> 00:20:14,500
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

371
00:20:19,067 --> 00:20:20,100
Are you okay now?

372
00:20:20,233 --> 00:20:23,000
Shouldn't you still be
recovering in the hospital?

373
00:20:23,267 --> 00:20:24,667
I'm fine, Joey.

374
00:20:25,767 --> 00:20:28,933
I found out what Zoey did
to you at the hospital,

375
00:20:29,067 --> 00:20:30,567
that's why I came here.

376
00:20:30,700 --> 00:20:32,367
It's nothing, it's okay.

377
00:20:33,567 --> 00:20:34,967
It actually helped

378
00:20:35,100 --> 00:20:38,933
because I was able to focus
on more important things.

379
00:20:39,100 --> 00:20:41,400
On what things?

380
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:44,867
Well, Jin Ho...

381
00:20:46,133 --> 00:20:49,467
I suspect he had something
to do with the attack on you.

382
00:20:49,600 --> 00:20:51,867
So, what we'll do now
is meet him,

383
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:54,433
then corner him
so he'll confess.

384
00:20:54,567 --> 00:20:59,467
- [CAR CHIMES]
- [HONKING]

385
00:20:59,600 --> 00:21:09,567
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

386
00:21:11,300 --> 00:21:14,700
And where are you going?

387
00:21:14,833 --> 00:21:17,067
You know,
my friends rescheduled.

388
00:21:17,200 --> 00:21:18,633
I'm just meeting them now.

389
00:21:18,767 --> 00:21:20,833
Okay, have fun.

390
00:21:20,967 --> 00:21:27,833
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

391
00:21:27,967 --> 00:21:35,267
- [CAR ENGINE STARTS]
- [FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

392
00:21:35,400 --> 00:21:36,533
Back in the car.

393
00:21:36,667 --> 00:21:38,233
We'll follow someone.

394
00:21:38,367 --> 00:21:43,833
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

395
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:45,600
Wait, wait, Joey.

396
00:21:45,733 --> 00:21:51,067
You're saying he's dangerous,
and you're going to see him?

397
00:21:51,200 --> 00:21:54,133
You and Peter?
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

398
00:21:54,267 --> 00:21:55,667
We have a plan.

399
00:21:55,800 --> 00:21:58,400
Joey, you're being immature
again.

400
00:21:59,567 --> 00:22:01,600
You're being reckless again.

401
00:22:01,733 --> 00:22:04,533
How is that reckless?
We have a plan.

402
00:22:04,667 --> 00:22:05,867
We thought this through.

403
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:07,333
Why don't you listen
to me first?

404
00:22:07,467 --> 00:22:09,167
Joey, why don't you listen
to me?

405
00:22:10,200 --> 00:22:12,267
Joey, stop this.

406
00:22:12,400 --> 00:22:15,200
But, Andrew, I want to catch
the people who hurt you.

407
00:22:15,367 --> 00:22:17,400
It's not necessary.

408
00:22:17,533 --> 00:22:19,367
So, we'll just let them go?

409
00:22:19,500 --> 00:22:21,533
Okay, if you're feeling
guilty...

410
00:22:21,667 --> 00:22:23,367
It's not guilt!

411
00:22:23,833 --> 00:22:29,100
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

412
00:22:29,233 --> 00:22:31,833
You don't understand how I feel.

413
00:22:34,400 --> 00:22:37,767
I thought you were going
to die when I held you?

414
00:22:39,833 --> 00:22:41,167
That's why I want to catch them.

415
00:22:41,300 --> 00:22:43,400
They need to pay
for what they did to you.

416
00:22:44,567 --> 00:22:46,067
Joey...

417
00:22:46,200 --> 00:22:47,133
That's enough.

418
00:22:47,267 --> 00:22:48,933
What if they come back?

419
00:22:50,833 --> 00:22:53,067
What if they do something worse
to you?

420
00:22:54,100 --> 00:22:56,100
Andrew, I don't want that
to happen.

421
00:22:56,233 --> 00:22:59,300
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

422
00:22:59,433 --> 00:23:02,333
I won't allow that
to happen to you...

423
00:23:02,467 --> 00:23:05,700
-Joey, stop.
-because you're important to me.

424
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:10,800
- Joey, stop, okay?
- Because I love you.

425
00:23:10,933 --> 00:23:13,933
[ROMANTIC MUSIC PLAYING]

426
00:23:14,067 --> 00:23:16,267
I love you, Andrew.

427
00:23:16,400 --> 00:23:26,367
[ROMANTIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

428
00:23:29,333 --> 00:23:34,100
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

429
00:23:34,233 --> 00:23:36,833
I'm also doing this for dad,
for my family.

430
00:23:36,967 --> 00:23:39,933
I just really want those
syndicates caught.

431
00:23:41,267 --> 00:23:42,467
- Joey!
- Jin Ho...

432
00:23:42,600 --> 00:23:43,967
Why did you have Andrew
beaten up?

433
00:23:44,100 --> 00:23:45,667
I don't know
what you're talking about.

434
00:23:45,800 --> 00:23:46,733
Give me the gun.

435
00:23:46,867 --> 00:23:48,200
You were the only one who knew

436
00:23:48,333 --> 00:23:50,633
we were going there that night.
Right?

437
00:23:50,767 --> 00:23:51,800
Just tell us.

438
00:23:51,933 --> 00:23:54,733
Where are the syndicates hiding?
And who is Berdugo?

439
00:23:54,900 --> 00:23:57,200
Joey, maybe we should hear
Jin Ho out first.

440
00:23:57,333 --> 00:23:59,867
So, you want to know the truth?
Fine, I'll tell you.
